It depends on the game. If I play nethack I play ASCII only. Simple reason I
know what everything looks like. I've played angband as well and there was a
decent tile set for one of the versions, but once again I preferred ASCII,
although in that game I prefer that the floor, walls and such be grapical.

Your best bet for popularity is to include both, and support for people
putting in there own tilesets. That way people who like ASCII will be happy
and people who like grapics will be happy. Then someone will come along and
do an excelent tileset for your game and that will increase it's popularity.



